  "known_blockers": [
    "The v24 global surface removes the dominant planar walls and open endpoint gap, but smooth or under-authored landforms remain visible in the fixed-camera set.",
    "Source-backed canopy preservation reaches 97.2670% in the visible strong-source band, but sparse/card vegetation and simplistic tree assets remain below the requested photoreal standard.",
    "Balanced solver-conditioned foam removes the broad pale rapid carpet, v675 adds up to 0.2624 m of bounded solver-resolved crest/hole relief with zero response on linear-grade or calm water, M9B.3 v24 replaces the cracked cellular breakup with project-owned solver-masked flow-aligned fragments, and v25 makes solver/contact-derived spray, mist and droplets smaller, denser and less opaque. M9B.3 v48 adds a separate non-colliding 8-by-8 curled sheet at each real hydraulic jump; the Meat Grinder window activates five sites and 640 triangles under a 3,072-triangle cap. The surrounding riverbed/terrain seams, hard water-patch boundaries, simplified crest shape, clean laces and analytic aerosol remain below final live-water art standards.",
    "Five packaged, independently morphed MakeHuman/MPFB bodies replace the Manny fallback and provide coherent rigged human anatomy, skin/eye atlases, finite rescue poses, and v579 weighted Hair02 geometry with item-level CC BY 4.0 attribution. Renderer review still rejects limited faces, fallback groom quality, generic wetsuits, and procedural PPE/body integration as final photoreal character art.",
    "The M9B.3 v13 production rescue-PFD replaces all four procedural vest layers with one project-owned 21,180-triangle, five-section asset across all five production MetaHuman wrappers. Its four-panel front, thin back, side wings, continuous shoulders, pockets, front entry, backup webbing and buckles, eight adjustment points, quick-release belt, tether ring, reflective zones, placard and lash tabs use the project-owned 1K PfdRipstop texture set and retain exactly 0.0 cm maximum measured torso-origin error. The asset is accepted technically, but the swept shoulders and broad front surfacing still read as procedural at portrait distance and fail final photoreal art review.",
    "The M9B.3 v34 production river boot replaces ten blunt procedural footwear overlays with a project-owned 9,708-triangle lasted source mesh, three material sections, twelve outsole lugs, three vamp bands, a 1,704-triangle Nanite fallback and collisionless solved-foot placement. Dedicated project-owned textured-neoprene and rubber materials preserve a dark footwear read while separating upper, sole and rand response. It is accepted as a reproducible silhouette, material and integration upgrade, but generated surface detail, rigid yaw-only placement and surrounding body/pose deformation remain below final photoreal character-art standards.",
    "The M9B.3 v35 production MetaHuman adapter caches the complete reference skeleton and applies deterministic thumb, metacarpal and finger articulation to both hands on all five avatars. Matched and contact-side renderer evidence shows stable attached digit chains and a firmer paddle-bearing hand shape without changing solved hands, paddles, crew mass, water, raft, collision, rescue or progression. The generic curl profile, coarse hand mesh, residual shaft spacing and procedural stroke biomechanics remain below final photoreal character-animation standards.",
    "The M9B.3 v36 production MetaHuman adapter treats each existing visible-paddle hand point as a middle-palm grip target and derives the skeletal wrist from the reference hand-to-palm offset. Exact M5 gates every rendered production avatar to at most 0.25 cm palm-anchor error, and matched/contact-side renderer evidence shows the shaft crossing the curled palm region without wrist, sleeve or digit detachment. Shared wrist orientation, generic curl, coarse hand topology and procedural stroke biomechanics remain below final photoreal character-animation standards.",
    "The M9B.3 v12 production-raft pass replaces the parametric rest silhouette with project-owned 38,344-triangle authored geometry while keeping it collisionless and D4-deformable. Kicked ends, chamber seams, two thwarts, an inflated floor, perimeter line, reinforcement, D-rings, quarter handles, valves, and drain recesses now follow the ordinary contact field. v42 makes the chamber cross-section consume existing D4 compression and transforms its tangent frame with the analytic deformation gradient without changing the hidden hull, collision, buoyancy, flip, wrap, pin, damage, or rescue authority. The later v43 wet-film bracket retained the oversized white band and made the foreground coating harsher, while v44 contact creases were not materially visible from matched or contact-port views; both were fully removed and the v42 source/material graph was rebuilt. Renderer review still rejects the broad synthetic tube response, crew contact/pose, boulder, planar broad water, procedural foam/aerosol, coarse shoreline, terrain, foliage, and lighting as final photoreal art.",
    "The M9B.3 v20 production-river-boulder pass replaces the 1,632-triangle runtime presentation shell with a project-owned 81,920-triangle closed asset and dedicated wet-mineral material while retaining the old shell as a load-failure fallback. The collisionless mesh is fitted to 96% of the existing radius; D4 radius, friction, contacts, wrap and pin authority are unchanged. Renderer review still rejects its large-scale mottling, broad facets and non-site-specific appearance as final photoreal rock art.",
    "The first v517 Shipping performance minute passed at 15.649 ms p95, but the independent confirmation minute crashed with SIGSEGV in the D3 overwash response-map rehash. v517 is superseded. The allocation-free repair passes 20,000 native evaluations, two v520 offscreen stability soaks, and two v527 normal-window Metal stability soaks. Six additional v527 -RenderOffScreen diagnostics were variable (three pass, three fail on wall-clock hitches), so that tooling path is explicitly not qualified as release performance.",
    "The exact-current V10 local technical chain is green: M4 v431 passes 4/4, M5 v432 5/5, M7 v433 4/4, M8 v434 4/4, and reconciled fail-closed M9 v437 5/5. The v436 Python/data/source matrix reports 1,146 passes, three expected installed-dependency-path skips, one intentional historical-v42 visual-source hash mismatch, and zero unexpected failures. V9 stock Niagara Fluids reuse remains rejected and removed. V10 supplies a visible project-owned six-frame closed implicit-volume cache with 104.89 cm generated depth, but it remains opt-in, default-off, presentation-only, photoreal-rejected, unapproved by named water-VFX art and South Fork guide reviewers, and unpromoted. The v670 settled 24-of-24 zero-modified HLOD evidence remains content-current because V10 promotes no runtime asset or map. Shipping/package/performance/archive evidence remains historical and non-promotable; a fresh clean rebuild, package, soak, archive, and qualification are still required after an accepted photoreal candidate.",
    "No capture is approved for marketing, store use, or the press kit."
  ],
